The two bags are heavy.
I walk home slowly.
I see a bakery on the corner.
I have no bread in the kitchen.
I open the door and go into the bakery.
The woman behind the counter smiles.
"Hello!"
"What would you like?" she asks.
"Hello, I would like a dark loaf of bread, please," I say.
The woman takes the bread from the shelf.
"Would you like anything else?" she asks.
I see a crusty Brötchen behind the glass.
I like Brötchen a lot.
I point at the Brötchen.
"I would also like that Brötchen there, please," I say.
That is perfect for my lunch.
"Would you like a coffee too?" the woman asks.
"No thank you, I do not want a coffee," I answer.
"That comes to four Euro and eighty Cents, please," she says.
I pay and take the bread and the Brötchen.
Now my shopping is complete.
